hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1020","Saeed bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Makhzoumi told us, and Ali bin Khashram told us. Saeed told us, and Ali said: Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, h. Amr bin Ali told us, Abu Asim told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, Ibn Shihab told us, H. Bundar told us, Othman told us Ibn Umar, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, and Muhammad Ibn Rafi’ narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudaik narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The devil comes to one of you while he is in prayer.” So his prayer is confused for him so that he does not know how many times he has prayed. So whoever finds any of that, let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting. And this is the meaning of the report. Yahya bin Abi Kathir, and Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Until the man remains He knows how many times he has prayed, three or four, so let him prostrate two times while sitting.”"
"1021","And in the report of Iyad, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “If he made a mistake and does not know how many times he has prayed, let him prostrate two prostrations while he was “Sitting.”"
"1022","And in the report of Iyad, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “If he made a mistake and does not know how many times he has prayed, let him prostrate two prostrations.” And he was sitting.” And in the news of Abdullah bin Jafar and Muawiyah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever has doubts about his prayer, let him prostrate two prostrations while he is \"Sitting.\" I mentioned these reports with their chains of transmission in the Book of Al-Kabir, and this wording is brief and not traceable."
